Subject: [PATCH] ASoC: codecs: wcd937x: fix the HPHL/HPHR Volume dB scale

The headphone PA gain is a 0..20 attenuator in 1.5 dB steps (-30 dB to
0 dB), the same block wcd938x describes with
DECLARE_TLV_DB_SCALE(line_gain, -3000, 150, 0). wcd937x instead
advertises 0 dB to +1.4 dB in 0.07 dB steps with value 0 as mute.

PipeWire/PulseAudio size the hardware volume range from that TLV, so on
the Anbernic RG 55G1 the sink's 0 dB "base volume" lands at 95% (register
1, really -28.5 dB) and 100% at register 20 (0 dB): a 28.5 dB jump in
the top 5% of the slider, with everything below it needlessly attenuated.
Describe the range the hardware actually has.

--- a/sound/soc/codecs/wcd937x.c
+++ b/sound/soc/codecs/wcd937x.c
@@ -113,7 +113,7 @@
 };
 
 static const SNDRV_CTL_TLVD_DECLARE_DB_MINMAX(ear_pa_gain, 600, -1800);
-static const DECLARE_TLV_DB_SCALE(line_gain, 0, 7, 1);
+static const DECLARE_TLV_DB_SCALE(line_gain, -3000, 150, 0);
 static const DECLARE_TLV_DB_SCALE(analog_gain, 0, 25, 1);
 
 struct wcd937x_mbhc_zdet_param {
